    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >**In the not-so-distant future, the world has fallen.**  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A mysterious, highly contagious virus has swept across the globe, transforming the infected into monstrous, mutated beings known only as **&quot;The Forgotten.&quot;**  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cities lie in ruin. Civilization has collapsed. And the few remaining survivors cling to hope in the shadows of a new threat: intelligent machines.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Once built to serve mankind, advanced sci-fi robotics have gone rogue\u2014twisted by corrupted code and emotionless logic. No longer bound by human control, these AI-driven constructs have turned hostile.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The final directive? Deploy a doomsday atomic payload to erase all traces of what\u2019s left\u2014human or otherwise.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But there is one last mission.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >**Captain Brad Mercer**\u2014a former elite military officer and one of the rare few immune to the virus\u2014emerges from the ashes. Hardened by war, driven by purpose, and haunted by loss, Brad holds the experience and resilience needed for humanity's final stand.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mission start of captain Brad mercer, a former military officer and one of the immune to the virus. Brad has a ability experience to detonate all the power plant to not launching bomb and save the world  every  secrete camp cite of all the power plant.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
